WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:06.060
This hateful son-of-a-birch is the deadliest
tree in the world.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:12.180
The Spanish call it “manzanilla de la muerte”
meaning “little apple of death”, its scientific

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:19.369
name is “Hippomane mancinella” which translates
to “little apple that makes horses mad”.

00:00:19.369 --> 00:00:24.180
But its real name is the Manchineel Tree and
it actually holds the Guinness World Record

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.890
for the world’s most dangerous tree.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:32.079
The menacing Manchineel can be found in the
Caribbean, Florida, Mexico, and all across

00:00:32.079 --> 00:00:33.440
South America.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:38.010
The tree is like an angry pot boiling over
with hatred and childhood issues, life can

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:40.120
be tough as a young sapling you know.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.829
Each part of the tree wants to kill you in
a different, agonising way.

00:00:43.829 --> 00:00:49.000
The fruits it grows look like apples, smell
like apples and even taste like apples, but

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.329
they’re not apples.

00:00:50.329 --> 00:00:54.550
Take a bite into a Manchineel fruit and you’ll
be like, this is alright, it tastes like apple

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:58.969
pie, but then you’ll be hit with an intense
peppery heat, that will quickly surge throughout

00:00:58.969 --> 00:01:04.739
your entire body causing intense pain and
severe burning for hours.

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:08.910
Your internal organs will start to bleed,
your throat will close up, restricting your

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:11.720
breathing and then death will soon follow.

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:17.620
Phew that escalated from sweet to savoury
pretty fast, but here’s the worst part,

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:21.510
the fruits are the LEAST toxic part of the
Manchineel tree.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:26.400
There’s a lot more ways this twiney twit
wants to turn you into driftwood.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.350
The tree’s main source of poison is from
its deadly sap.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:33.620
Its branches constantly ooze out a sticky
white substance.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:39.170
If just a drop of this touches your skin it
will burn right through it like acid, causing

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:41.230
blisters and agonising pain.

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:47.510
If the sap gets in your eyes it can cause
permanent blindness and just like every other

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:52.630
part of this sadistic tree, if you inhale
it or if the sap enters your bloodstream,

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:54.250
it will kill you.

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:58.440
The aboriginal people of the Caribbean used
the tree to their advantage, they used the

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:03.140
sap of the Manchineel to make poison arrows
which were extremely effective.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:09.039
Famous Spanish conquistador Juan Ponce de
Leon was actually killed by an arrow poisoned

00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:10.409
with Manchineel sap.

00:02:10.409 --> 00:02:15.410
During his final voyage to Florida to establish
a settlement, in a battle with the Native

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:22.099
American Calusa people, he took a Manchineel-poisoned
arrow to the knee, well it was his thigh actually.

00:02:22.099 --> 00:02:25.879
He escaped the battle but died soon after
from the poison.

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:31.489
But you don’t even need to touch the Manchineel
tree to suffer its deadly consequences.

00:02:31.489 --> 00:02:36.129
When it rains the sap is washed off the leaves
and branches and is dispersed all around the

00:02:36.129 --> 00:02:37.579
tree via rainwater.

00:02:37.579 --> 00:02:43.590
Therefore, if you stand under a Manchineel
tree whilst it’s raining your entire body

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:48.220
will quickly burn up and perish like every
talent-show winner’s career and you’ll

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:51.690
be left with blisters, burns and scars all
over.

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:56.060
Many beach going tourists have suffered horrific
injuries whilst seeking cover from the rain

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:59.819
underneath a Manchineel tree, unbeknownst
to its dangers.

00:02:59.819 --> 00:03:05.530
Also, if you burn the bark of the Manchineel
tree the smoke that is produced is so toxic

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:09.760
that it will permanently blind anyone standing
nearby.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:15.749
In fact, this angry wooden bugger is so toxic
that simply standing near it for a prolonged

00:03:15.749 --> 00:03:21.790
period of time can cause serious injuries
and possibly death via asphyxiation, as your

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:27.230
throat closes up, caused by just breathing
in the tree’s toxic scent.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:32.080
Something or someone has seriously ticked
off this psychopathic tree, it’s as if you

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:37.670
came onto its patch on Christmas day and slapped
it silly with its own sapling babies, it was

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:40.869
you wasn’t it, shame on you, you dirty tree-slapper.

